# models/
#
# Data-access layer for each table. Since we use raw SQL via the pg pool
# (not an ORM), each model file holds the queries for one table, e.g.:
#   - farmer.model.ts   -> findById, create, update, delete...
#
# Use the typed query<T>() helper from db/pool.ts so rows come back typed.
# Keeping queries here (not scattered in controllers) means schema changes
# touch one file. Schemas WILL evolve - this isolation is what makes that safe.
